course: dictionary
lesson: 682
title: A word for a pen
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A ballpoint is a pen with a tiny metal ball at its tip. The ball rolls and spreads ink onto the paper as you write. «A ballpoint pen has a tiny metal ball at its tip» tells you what it is, and the words around it give you the clues.
explain: Ballpoint can also be a describing word, an adjective, as in «ballpoint ink». Here it tells you what kind of ink it is: ink that comes from a ballpoint pen. Ask yourself, what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: The sentence also gives a clue about how the pen works: the ink «needs to flow down to the ball», so most ballpoints stop working upside down. The ball is what puts the ink on the paper.
fact: A ballpoint is a pen with a tiny metal ball at its tip.
fact: The ball rolls and spreads ink onto the paper as you write.
fact: As an adjective, ballpoint describes the ink or the pen: «ballpoint ink».
fact: Ballpoint ink cannot be rubbed out like pencil.
fact: In the UK, a ballpoint is often called a biro.
exercise: What is a ballpoint? | A ruler made of metal | A brush that paints with water | *A pen with a tiny metal ball at its tip that rolls and spreads ink | A pencil with a rubber on the end
exercise: «A ballpoint pen has a tiny metal ball at its tip» — what is the tiny metal ball for? | To make the pen heavier | *To roll ink from the tube onto the paper | To hold the pen up straight | To rub out mistakes
exercise: Someone in the UK asks for a biro. What do they want? | *A ballpoint pen | A paint pen for a poster | A wooden pencil | A marker for whiteboards
test: In «ballpoint ink», what does ballpoint tell you? | The ink is dark and thick like paint | The ink is made from pencil lead | *The ink comes from a pen with a tiny metal ball at its tip | A kind of ink that is rubbed out with a rubber
test: Why do most ballpoints stop working upside down? | The metal ball falls out | Ballpoint pens are too small to hold | The ink is too heavy | *The ink needs to flow down to the ball
exam: Which word means a pen with a tiny metal ball at its tip? | paintbrush | *ballpoint | pencil | crayon
